{
  "issue": {
    "number": 4232,
    "title": "Text.from_ansi exposes OSC 8 payloads with BEL-terminated hyperlinks",
    "state": "closed",
    "created_at": "2026-10-02T10:21:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-02T20:04:49Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues/4232",
    "labels": [],
    "body": "- [x] I've checked the docs and searched open and closed issues for OSC/BEL/terminator reports.\n- [x] I've checked the FAQ; this reproduction uses the recommended `Text.from_ansi` conversion.\n\n**The bug**\n\n`Text.from_ansi` exposes OSC 8 payload text and loses the link when the sequence ends with BEL. The equivalent ST-terminated sequence works.\n\n```python\nfrom rich.text import Text\n\nfor terminator in (\"\\x1b\\\\\", \"\\x07\"):\n    source = f\"\\x1b]8;;https://example.com{terminator}hello\\x1b]8;;{terminator}\"\n    text = Text.from_ansi(source)\n    print(repr(text.plain), [(s.start, s.end, str(s.style)) for s in text.spans])\n```\n\nActual output:\n\n```text\n'hello' [(0, 5, 'link https://example.com')]\n'8;;https://example.comhello8;;' []\n```\n\nExpected: both inputs produce plain text `hello` with the same link span. Xterm documents both BEL and ST as OSC terminators: https://invisible-island.net/xterm/ctlseqs/ctlseqs.html#h3-Operating-System-Commands\n\n`re_ansi` in `rich/ansi.py` currently recognizes ST for its OSC branch, but not BEL. This is distinct from #3561, which measures raw ANSI strings without converting them first.\n\n**Platform**\n\nCurrent main commit `9d8f9a3`, Python 3.14.6, macOS arm64. Reproduced from the checkout with markdown-it-py and Pygments installed via uv. No terminal rendering is needed to reproduce this.\n\nAI assistance (Codex) was used to investigate and prepare this report; the output above was verified locally. No PR is attached.\n"
  },
